Z||000000||Shawn85SE||02-13-2000||12:24 PM||||I came across this site and was just wondering if anyone has used them before.It looks like they have alot of stuff.||||reg||5
Z||000001||GREENDANO||02-13-2000||12:32 PM||||I've tried to e-mail them 3 times in the last week and I got no responses.  I haven't called, but if they won't repond to e-mail as a general rule I won't do business with them.  Yes, lots of parts, just be an educated consumer.  Some of their stuff is priced very reasonably, while other stuff is off the meter!!!<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||02-13-2000||12:39 PM||||I've only done business with them a couple of times. But I have been very pleased with the service I recieved. Parts I ordered were in the good condition, pricing was reasonable, and they have parts I can't find anywhere else. I would do service with them again, and do recommend them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||02-13-2000||03:28 PM||||What "56" said...<BR>I've heard that they are not really "computer savvy", and don't deal with e-mail, too much. I called them on the phone, and they were very helpful. Although they did sound VERY busy, they took the time to answer my questions. You might get a lot of busy signals, or ring-no-answer. Keep trying. I placed a credit card order, and got my item in about 3-4 days. Be sure to compare for price, as well. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||02-13-2000||04:47 PM||||I emailed them last summer to get a price on a driver's seat for my 88 Coupe last summer and got a quick response.  I ordered the seat by phone using VISA and got my seat in 3 days.<P>Then, a couple of months later, I emailed to get pricing on some body parts for my 86 SE and got no response, so I wound up buying them from another Forum member.  I was a little peeved at the ignored email since I'd bought from them before.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||02-13-2000||09:48 PM||||Called them last Thursday for a replacement door glass for my GT. Got it the following Teusday and was packed very well! So far I'm very pleased with them.||||reg||14
Z||000006||GWMORGAN||02-13-2000||10:19 PM||||I'v ordered from them 5 times and they always deliver on time.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Brian84SE||02-13-2000||10:33 PM||||Living in CT, I took a ride to Kick Hill.  Very interesting place.  A 2 story barn filled with fiero parts.   Talk about heaven!   In another room, he had a Vietnam era helicopter he is restoring.  Like a said, very interesting!<P>The guy was great to talk to, and gave me exellent prices.  I would certainly recommend him.||||reg||1
Z||000008||cobra427||02-14-2000||11:56 PM||||In addition to having a million and one parts he also has a restorable Zimmer in one of his garages. A really nice and very busy guy.<P>For thos that maybe interested, a tentative date of noon, March 11, at Kick Hill,will be a time set aside to try and reorganize a new New England Fiero club.<BR> I believe that Kick Hill will be sponsoring this meet.If there are questions, feel free to contact me at cobra@c4.net||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||02-15-2000||04:11 AM||||Hey Cobra, I just got the info on the meet and I wasn't sure if you had received it yet so I forwarded you the info I got. I'll try like hell to be there. I'm psyched we may now have a reputable club here in N.E.||||reg||10
